  abstract = {The objective of this research is to analyze comparatively the environmental behavior of the green consumer between Mexico, Colombia and Brazil from an approach of the constructs environmental knowledge, environmental affect, ecological concern and the behavior of green purchases, by means of a quantitative descriptive study carried out in over 18 years old and residing in the urban area of Ribeir\~ao Preto and Piracicaba in the state of S\~ao Paulo in Brazil, in Mexico over 18 years old and residing in the urban area of Puebla and Tlaxcala in Mexico and recently in the cities from Bogot\'a and Cartagena in Colombia. In total, 423 young people were chosen according to the criteria of convenience, in all countries. The data collection necessary for the description of the results was based on the analysis or study described by Malhotra (2001) simple cross-sectional method. In general terms, similar results were found in this study between Colombia, Mexico and Brazil, the requirements in the measurement of the multiple correlation between independent variables (environmental knowledge, ecological concern and environmental affect) and the dependent variable (CCCE). It presents an environmental behavior that does not correspond too much with its level of knowledge in this respect, since the variations between knowing and applying knowledge is very dispersed.},
